/Title (Monthly revenue performance was primarily driven by sales volume, as total units sold showed the strongest correlation with revenue \(r = 0.91\). Additionally, total transactions also had a strong relationship with revenue \(r = 0.81\).)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2317 0 R
/Next 2493 0 R
>>
endobj
2493 0 obj
<<
/Title (Average product value showed minimal correlation with revenue, suggesting that revenue fluctuations were less influenced by product pricing)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2317 0 R
/Prev 2492 0 R
>>
endobj
2494 0 obj
<<
/Title (Units Sold is the strongest driver of monthly revenue performance. The regression model explains 83.1% of the variation in monthly revenue \(F = 49.05, p < 0.001\).)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2286 0 R
/Prev 2318 0 R
/Next 2539 0 R
>>
endobj
2495 0 obj
<<
